cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its result files, please cite this repository and the associated article."
title: "Iterative Temporal Regression Imputation (ITRI) and Cross-Feature Residual Interpolation (CFRI) for contiguous missing blocks in multivariate financial time series: code, protocols, and results"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "KOTAN"
    given-names: "Kurban"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6660-0565"
    affiliation: "Manisa Celal Bayar University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kurbankotan/itri-financial-time-series-imputation"
url: "https://github.com/kurbankotan/itri-financial-time-series-imputation"
license: MIT
version: "2.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - missing data imputation
  - financial time series
  - contiguous missing blocks
  - temporal regression
  - cross-feature residual interpolation
  - external validation
  - distribution shift
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocols, condition-level results, tables, and figures for a
  leakage-aware window and pass ablation of Iterative Temporal Regression
  Imputation on BIST 30 and S&P 500 data, matched-mask comparators on the same
  data, an external validation on 34 country ETFs against linear
  interpolation, PCHIP, KNN, chained ridge, BRITS, and SAITS, including an
  exploratory configuration sweep, a level-shift diagnostic, and a per-window
  normalization amendment, and the cross-feature residual interpolation
  extension with its prespecified test on January to September 2026 data and
  its locally frozen holdout on 16 new ETFs with a peer-return bridge.
